*  148 - Minimal *var FENCE in ARBNO with seal-required backtrack.
*  Tightest variant of the 119/129 bug class — input string 'ab', not 'aab'.
*  If seal holds: ARBNO matches 'a' (cursor 0->1), tail RPOS(0) wants
*  cursor=2.  Backtrack into FENCE-sealed alts must be blocked, so
*  match fails and GOOD branch fires.
        cmd   = FENCE('a' | 'ab')
        outer = ARBNO(*cmd)
        s     = 'ab'
        s POS(0) *outer RPOS(0)                               :S(BAD)F(GOOD)
BAD     OUTPUT = 'leak: seal failed to block ab alt retry'    :(END)
GOOD    OUTPUT = 'seal blocks ab retry'
END
